Role of OLAP
OLAP (Online Analytical Processing) helps analyse academic performance across many views at
once. Marks are the measure, and subject, student, semester and department are the dimensions.
 - Roll-up: summarise to a higher level (subject averages to semester or department averages).
 - Drill-down: go from totals to detail (from semester average down to subject, then to a single
   student).
 - Slice and dice: pick one value or a sub-cube of the data (only the DBMS subject (slice), or DBMS
   and TOC for semester 5 (dice)).
 - Pivot: rotate the view to compare two dimensions side by side.
 - OLAP gives fast answers on large historical data, so decision makers can see trends without
   writing complex queries.
Conclusion: simple SQL (SELECT, aggregate functions, GROUP BY) gives the required reports,
and OLAP lets us analyse the same data from many angles.


